# THREAD B stage 3 -- successive minima: the CORRECT finiteness ruler
##################################################################################

==================================================================================
PART A -- exact l_infty successive minima  lambda_1 <= ... <= lambda_{d-1}
==================================================================================
  Relation lattice covolume = ||speeds||_2 (primitive); prod(minima) ~ covolume ~ span.
  shape                             d-1             minima (l_inf) lam_max   ||s||2  span   measS7
  consec8 {0..7}                      6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]       1       11     7   0.3272
  {0..6,8}                            6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]       1       12     8   0.2083
  AP*2 {0,2..14}                      6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]       1       23    14   0.3272
  AP*3 {0,3..21}                      6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]       1       35    21   0.3272
  stranger {0..6,40}                  6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2]       2       41    40   0.1905
  Sidon {0,1,3,7,12,20,30,44}         6         [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]       1       58    44   0.0121
  geom {0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64}           6         [2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]       2       73    64   0.0692
  two-cluster {0,1,2,40,41,42,43}     5            [1, 1, 1, 1, 6]       6       83    43   0.0338

  READING: consec/AP have ALL minima small (totally low-height). Stranger/two-cluster
  have lambda_max LARGE (a dissociated direction). lambda_max is the finiteness ruler.

==================================================================================
PART B -- SPAN BOUND: lambda_max(E) <= H0  =>  span(E) bounded (finiteness)
==================================================================================
  THEOREM (to verify): for primitive E, span(E) <= product of minima <= (lambda_max)^{d-1}
  times a small constant.  More usefully measure: max span over primitive E with
  lambda_max <= H0.  If finite => the totally-low-height family is finite.

